SUMMARY:Deadline 13:00 GMT: Upe Foundation Curatorial Fellow at Gasworks 20
 27-2028 (London\, GBP 32\,000\, Baltic connection)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 09 Nov 2026 at 13:00 GMT.\n\nThe Upe Foundation and Gasw
 orks are recruiting a full-time Curatorial Fellow for 12 to 18 months\, em
 bedded in Gasworks' curatorial team in south London. The Fellow works clos
 ely with the artist selected for the 2027 Gasworks residency for artists b
 ased in the Baltics and co-develops their 2028 solo exhibition\, alongside
  wider exhibition\, registrar\, interpretation and residency duties.\n\nOr
 ganisation: Upe Foundation (in partnership with Gasworks)\nLocation: Londo
 n\, UK. For early-career curators with a connection to the Baltic region (
 Lithuania\, Latvia\, Estonia or their diasporas)\; Gasworks will consider 
 visa sponsorship.\nAward: GBP 32\,000 per year salary\, 5% employer pensio
 n contribution\, relocation flights up to GBP 250 where relevant\, visa sp
 onsorship considered. No application fee.\nDuration: Full-time fixed-term 
 fellowship of 12 to 18 months\, spanning the 2027 residency and 2028 solo 
 exhibition.\n\nMore: https://gasworks.org.uk/opportunities/upe-foundation-
 curatorial-fellow?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referra
 l
URL:https://gasworks.org.uk/opportunities/upe-foundation-curatorial-fellow?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:London\, UK. For early-career curators with a connection to the Ba
 ltic region (Lithuania\, Latvia\, Estonia or their diasporas)\; Gasworks w
 ill consider visa sponsorship.
END:VEVENT
